  "hints": [
    "The API should only enqueue. Who does the slow downloading, and where does it put the pages?",
    "4,500 fetches/s arrive. Workers must remove at least that many, with headroom.",
    "LB (2) → API (6) → Kafka → Fetchers (4) → S3, plus API → Redis → NoSQL for seen-URL checks."
  ],
  "scoring": {
    "weights": {
      "performance": 0.35,
      "reliability": 0.3,
      "cost": 0.15,
      "architecture": 0.2
    },
    "latencyTargetMs": 40,
    "costBudget": 2300
  },
  "explanation": [
    "The frontier is a durable log (Kafka) partitioned by host, so each fetcher handles one site at a time and stays polite.",
    "Fetchers scale horizontally; size them to outrun the frontier or the backlog grows forever.",
    "Dedup with a fast seen-set (a cache or Bloom filter) in front of the URL index before scheduling a fetch."
  ]
